    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0988" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg884"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Treasury Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant
                        to the Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1944-09-25" notBefore="1944-09-13T20:00:00-04:00"
                            >undated</date>.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d566-f1"/>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the Secretary’s
                        Files</hi></p>
                <p>Dinner at the Citadel, Quebec, Wednesday, September 13, 1944, 8:00 p.m.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>However, the President came back to the German problem several times very nicely
                    and did not recede from his position. He reminded Churchill that Stalin at
                    Teheran had said: “Are you going to let Germany produce modern metal furniture?
                    The manufacture of metal furniture can be quickly turned into the manufacture of
                        armament.”<anchor n="2" xml:id="d566-f2"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed>H. D. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d566-f1" n="1" xml:id="d566-f1-content">
                <p>The date “9/25/44” which appears at the end of the memorandum is evidently the
                    date of typing.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d566-f2" n="2" xml:id="d566-f2-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg511">p. 511</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
